<title>UK: U.S. army, marine corps to use British guns.</title>
<headline>U.S. army, marine corps to use British guns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S.Defence Department confirmed on Monday that GEC-Marine VSEL, together with partner Cadillac Gage as prime contractor, had been awarded a contract for production of lightweight 155 mm howitzers to be used by the U.S. Marine Corps and U.S. Army.</p>
<p>A British Defence Ministry statement said the contract was for a two-and-a-half year engineering, manufacturing and development phase.</p>
<p>The contract included an option for an initial production of 190 guns for the U.S. Marine Corps.</p>
<p>The U.S. Marine Corps and Army need a total of 1,000 howitzers, which could involve business of more than $1 billion.</p>
<p>It was not known how much of this would eventually be offered to the British firms.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
